™s heaviest air-polluting facilities, based on self-reported data shared with the EPA, operate without a single public air monitor within five miles.</p><p>This list includes Dow Chemicalâ€™s plastics factory in Plaquemine, which is about eight miles from the nearest air monitoring station. The station measures only ozone even though the plant releases an array of toxic pollutants including ethylene oxide, a known carcinogen.</p><p>No public monitors measure ammonia â€“ despite the fact that CF Industriesâ€™ Donaldsonville plant emits more than 7m lbs of the hazardous chemical each year, <a href="https://www.documentcloud.org/documents/28220631-largest-industrial-air-polluters-2024/">according to EPA data.</a></p><p>The three chemicals that researchers have concluded â€œtogether account for the large majority of <a href="https://www.pnas.org/doi/10.1073/pnas.2504770122">total cancer risk</a>â€ in the area â€“ ethylene oxide, chloroprene and formaldehyde â€“ arenâ€™t monitored by the state at all.</p> <a href="https://www.theguardian.com/environment/2026/jul/20/louisiana-toxic-air-floodlight">Continue reading...</a>ƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;6B-BADyPWtBxzheRXs48EVeaXfdZDMRRLusWoVEmGRgƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstardunit‚dmarkx9ni:///sha-256;DQxlflhKq0Y9c4QqH4GzHuNxSVtirPpk-qlhpLYE_kMƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;FZKYGKRu6jzUOZjXdvVHwZntVUUf7i1_zh_75_VrUm4ƒdpairƒdleftdstarƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitdunit‚dmark`ƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;uPKb0vXwEnrnyC37mEv0v28RDVw2GM5G4ZeAcCqZuGIƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstarƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitdunit‚dmarkefalseƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;fC3Ai56dfwSnnGUm4GAA_b6tT1THzoSF9El0hylJHPwƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstarƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitdunit‚dmarkdtrueƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni://